1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,880
This video shows you how to add a worker on a second machine to your leader.

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,430
Then you see both workers online.

3
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:13,270
Status shows the one worker your leader runs itself.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:16,568
A new worker joins with an enrollment code.

5
00:00:16,568 --> 00:00:20,643
In Admin, open Workers, then Enrollment codes.

6
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:23,662
Add a code for the standalone group.

7
00:00:23,662 --> 00:00:27,515
It brings in one worker, within twenty-four hours.

8
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:30,668
Mint it.

9
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,550
Check the address the worker reaches the leader at.

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,356
Then copy these lines.

11
00:00:37,356 --> 00:00:39,910
They're shown only this once.

12
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:45,110
On the second machine, save them in a file named worker.env.

13
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:48,409
Start the worker from the same image as the leader,

14
00:00:48,409 --> 00:00:51,350
with that file, and a volume for its state.

15
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,156
Its logs show it enrolled.

16
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:59,614
The code names the leader's certificate authority,

17
00:00:59,614 --> 00:01:02,990
so the worker takes that one, and accepts no other.

18
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:08,702
Back on Status, the standalone group has two workers, both online.

19
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:15,430
They're in one group, so both run its pipelines, at the same commit.

20
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,284
Check on learning.

21
00:01:17,484 --> 00:01:20,035
The leader signed its own certificate.

22
00:01:20,035 --> 00:01:22,851
Why does the new worker trust it?

23
00:01:27,251 --> 00:01:31,076
Its enrollment code names the leader's certificate authority,

24
00:01:31,076 --> 00:01:33,996
and the worker accepts only that one.

25
00:01:34,896 --> 00:01:38,578
Next, you build your first pipeline.
